From 63e3decdc5835c58fece2ecb6a29d5c2e6380313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kurtvan <kurtv7348@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:10:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Draw caller textures into the frame at fixed layers

Adds projectm_set_layer_texture(instance, layer, texture). The caller
prepares a texture completely (colour adjustments, masks, opacity as
straight alpha) and projectM only alpha-blends it in, keeping the
destination's alpha:

- PROJECTM_LAYER_FEEDBACK: into the previous-frame buffer before the
  warp, so the preset's warp distorts the image (e.g. live video) like
  its own.
- PROJECTM_LAYER_BEFORE_COMPOSITE: stored, not drawn yet.

Textures live on the ProjectM instance and are handed to whichever
preset is active, so they persist across preset loads. The blend program
and VAO are owned by the instance (LayerBlend), created on first use,
and restore the blend/program/VAO/texture state they change.
